& [PostP8ReadinessSurfaceV1] is the current readiness surface after P8 proof fixtures evaluation and faults acceptance
  + [surface_state] is ready_for_next_deeper_reasoning_design_selection
  + [accepted_boundary_input] is PostP4ReadinessSurfaceV1
  + [accepted_boundary_input] is P8ProofFixturesEvaluationFaultsFinalSliceSurfaceV1
  + [accepted_boundary_input] is P8BoundaryImportAndFixtureObligationInventoryV1
  + [accepted_boundary_input] is P8FixturePathPolicyAndGeneratedOutputNonpromotionContractV1
  + [accepted_boundary_input] is P8FixturePackMaterializationPlanAndImplementationActivationBoundaryV1
  + [accepted_boundary_input] is P8StaleFalseReadyContradictionAndFaultOraclePlanV1
  + [accepted_boundary_input] is P8ProofLedgerAndEvaluationAcceptanceContractV1
  + [active_implementation_chunk] is none
  + [current_ready_chunk] is P5 LangGraph procedure runtime final slice minting
  + [secondary_ready_chunk] is P6 surface projection expansion after P5 runtime authority and projection fixture authority are reminted
  + [secondary_ready_chunk] is P8 fixture material implementation activation after P5/P6 downstream consumption requirements are reviewed
  + [gated_chunk] is fixture source file creation until future source-preserved implementation activation explicitly opens files
  + [gated_chunk] is proof ledger file creation until future source-preserved implementation activation explicitly opens ledgers
  + [gated_chunk] is generated output creation until future ignored generated-output roots and proof runner contracts are accepted
  + [gated_chunk] is P7 dispatch-adjacent coordination expansion until dispatch authority is source-preserved and accepted
  + [gated_chunk] is P9 operations live-control reconsideration until separate source-preserved live-control authority is accepted
  + [gated_chunk] is dependency installation, package metadata mutation, adapters, transports, UI, assignment, dispatch, operations control, and live machine control until explicit accepted authority opens bounded work
  + [safety_limit] is no assignment, dispatch, operations control, or live machine control authorized

  = must: choose the next slice from current support, completed-work deltas, and whole-field dependency closure
  = must: run completion review after each new design, planning, proof, or implementation slice before opening downstream slices
  = must: preserve P8 fixture path policy, generated-output nonpromotion, proof ledger fields, accepted-absence proof, stale/rebake rules, negative oracle cases, and no-live-effect boundaries in downstream work
  = must: keep generated outputs, graph checkpoints, surface projections, packet candidates, and dry-run evidence non-authoritative unless accepted source authority explicitly says otherwise

& [ReadinessChunk: P5LangGraphProcedureRuntime] is ready_for_final_slice_minting
  + [chunk_id] is P5
  + [chunk_name] is LangGraph procedure runtime
  + [dependency_set] is P2 authority kernel and record schemas
  + [dependency_set] is P3 compiled SOP operator contracts
  + [dependency_set] is P8 proof ledger and fixture nonpromotion authority
  + [expected_output_set] is source-preserved P5 final slice surface
  + [expected_output_set] is graph procedure runtime boundary and checkpoint nonauthority contract
  + [expected_output_set] is SOP interrupt and human-judgment handoff contract
  + [expected_output_set] is fixture-backed graph proof shape without live graph execution effects
  + [model_route] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [model_route_reason] is LangGraph runtime authority depends on proof ledger support, checkpoint nonauthority, SOP interrupt semantics, and generated-output nonpromotion boundaries
  + [future_Spark_suitable_work] is GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable graph fixture implementation only after P5 final slices and source-preserved implementation activation accept exact graph contracts and fixture paths
  + [forbidden_scope] is dependency installation, package metadata mutation, adapter implementation, transport implementation, UI implementation, command execution outside validation, process control, GPU control, model runtime mutation, job dispatch, credential access or mutation, network exposure mutation, destructive filesystem action, persistent automation, operations control, and live machine control

  = must: source-preserve, SJS-process, and final-slice P5 before trusting runtime work as current authority
  = must: keep LangGraph checkpoint state non-authoritative and separate from SOP source authority, proof ledgers, generated outputs, and surface projections
  = must: include blocked, stale, contradicted, interrupted, faulted, rebake_required, and not_run paths in runtime proof planning

& [PostP8ProofAndFixtureStatus] is the accepted P8 status for downstream design
  + [fixture_obligation_inventory_status] is accepted_plan_only
  + [fixture_path_policy_status] is accepted_contract_only
  + [generated_output_nonpromotion_status] is accepted_contract_only
  + [fixture_materialization_boundary_status] is accepted_plan_only
  + [negative_oracle_status] is accepted_plan_only
  + [proof_ledger_acceptance_status] is accepted_contract_only
  + [fixture_material_creation_status] is not_authorized
  + [expected_ledger_creation_status] is not_authorized
  + [proof_ledger_creation_status] is not_authorized
  + [generated_output_creation_status] is not_authorized
  + [assignment_status] is not_authorized
  + [dispatch_status] is not_authorized
  + [operations_control_status] is not_authorized
  + [live_control_status] is not_authorized

  = must: require downstream P5 and P6 planning to consume P8 fixture path policy, generated-output nonpromotion, negative oracle, proof ledger, stale proof, rebake, and no-live-effect boundaries explicitly
  = must: mark downstream designs stale if P8 source, path policy, nonpromotion contract, proof ledger contract, fault oracle, completion review, or this readiness surface changes

& [PostP8ReadinessClosureReview] is the dependency audit for the post-P8 readiness surface
  + [P8-S01_status] is accepted
  + [P8-S02_status] is accepted
  + [P8-S03_status] is accepted
  + [P8-S04_status] is accepted
  + [P8-S05_status] is accepted
  + [P8_completion_status] is accepted_by docs/reviews/P8_Completion_Review.v1.sop
  + [current_ready_chunk_set] is P5 LangGraph procedure runtime final slice minting
  + [conditionally_ready_chunk_set] is P6 surface projection expansion after P5 final slice authority and projection fixture authority advance
  + [conditionally_ready_chunk_set] is P8 fixture material implementation activation after P5/P6 downstream consumption requirements are reviewed
  + [unresolved_external_dependency_set] is future P5 source-preserved final slice specification
  + [forbidden_external_dependency_found] is false
  + [fixture_source_file_creation_authorized] is false
  + [expected_ledger_creation_authorized] is false
  + [proof_ledger_creation_authorized] is false
  + [generated_output_creation_authorized] is false
  + [assignment_authorized] is false
  + [manager_dispatch_authorized] is false
  + [agent_dispatch_authorized] is false
  + [operations_control_authorized] is false
  + [live_machine_control_authorized] is false

  = must: treat P5 final slice minting as ready and deeper-reasoning required
  = must: treat implementation activation, fixture material creation, adapter work, transport work, UI work, dispatch authority, live-control authority, and downstream operations execution as gated, not ready
  = must: rerun closure review when a P8 boundary output changes, proof policy changes, or generated-output promotion contradiction appears
